## Why This Is Asked
Real-world multi-tenant data pipelines demand strong isolation, auditable control planes, and robust failure handling. This question probes identity management, data residency, and operational resilience in GCP.

## Key Concepts
- Partner-signed URLs for secure ingestion
- Cloud Functions validation and Pub/Sub as a decoupler
- Dataflow (streaming/batch) with per-tenant partitioning
- CMEK and tenant-scoped IAM + Workload Identity Federation
- VPC Service Controls perimeter to prevent exfiltration
- Idempotent processing and replay protection
- Rollback and test strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: publish validated message to Pub/Sub from a Cloud Function (Node.js)
const {PubSub} = require('@google-cloud/pubsub');
const pubsub = new PubSub();
exports.validateAndPublish = async (event) => {
  const record = JSON.parse(event.body);
  // basic schema check
  if (!record.tenant_id || !record.file_uri) throw new Error('Invalid');
  await pubsub.topic('tenant-ingest').publish(Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(record)));
};
```

